ld on Sunday, 2 June. Conditions: Mild at start with strong breeze. Very hot later with hot gusting wind the entire day. Runners had 12 hours to complete the course.\n\nClaude MOSHIYWA claimed the men's title in 05:32:09, ahead of Jonas BUUD (05:41:21) and Mpesela NTLOSOEU (05:43:38). Elena NURGALIEVA won the women's race in 06:27:09, followed by Olesya NURGALIEVA (06:28:07).\n\nElena NURGALIEVA's 06:27:09 was faster than the men's winning time as recently as 1959 (Trevor ALLEN, 06:28:11).\n\nFrom a field of 19,881 entries, 10,223 runners crossed the finish line (51.4% completion rate), with athletes representing over 19 countries. The field comprised 8,262 men and 1,960 women (19.2% female). The average finish time was 10:27:45.\n\nMedals awarded: 20 Gold, 3 Wally Hayward, 305 Silver, 1,378 Bill Rowan, 4,414 Bronze, 4,103 Vic Clapham. 2,371 runners (23.2%) were completing their first Comrades. The final finisher was Hilton MOKOKA in 11:59:56.\n\nVeterans and masters athletes made up 53% of the finishers, with 4,804 seniors (avg 10:16:25) and 5,417 in the veteran categories.","countryDataPct":100.0}